From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Domenico D'Arrigo <d.darrigo@outlook.it>
Date: Mon, 26 Oct 2026 01:28:11 +0100
Subject: [PATCH] nb/intel/haswell: Give the panel power at wake for its HPD

With gfx_resume_init off, the S3 resume path sets up the panel timings
and the backlight PWM and leaves the panel without power. An eDP panel
raises HPD only once it has power (T3), and macOS
(AppleIntelFramebufferAzul) reads the live HPD state of the panel port
at wake before it powers the panel up: it finds it low and keeps the
display off. With the option on, libgfxinit powers the panel up to probe
it, and HPD is high by the time the OS looks.

On the ThinkPad W541 under Linux, with the detection of the panel port
(DDI D) enabled, SDEISR bit 23 reads 1 with the panel powered and 0 with
it off (PP_STATUS and PP_CONTROL 0).

On that path, force VDD on, as an OS driver does to reach an eDP panel
over AUX while the panel is off, and wait for the power-up delay of the
panel (up_delay_ms). The power sequence and the backlight stay off, so
nothing shows. Linux takes the forced VDD over at resume ("VDD left on
by BIOS, adjusting state tracking") and turns it off when it no longer
needs it, whereas the power sequence left on would trip the "panel power
already on" warning of i915. An OS driver that never clears the override
leaves the panel with power until the next sleep, also with the display
off. Skip boards without a panel power sequence, and a panel that has
power already.

TEST=Built lenovo/w541 with mrc.bin and with the native RAM init.

Co-authored-by: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
Claude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_018n3yuWwDLW63F4vdf7ZFTv
---
 src/northbridge/intel/haswell/gma.c | 32 ++++++++++++++++++++++++++---
 1 file changed, 29 insertions(+), 3 deletions(-)

diff --git a/src/northbridge/intel/haswell/gma.c b/src/northbridge/intel/haswell/gma.c
index 578d5a4d3e..d30550a74f 100644
--- a/src/northbridge/intel/haswell/gma.c
+++ b/src/northbridge/intel/haswell/gma.c
@@ -413,6 +413,29 @@ static void gma_setup_panel(struct device *dev)
 	gtt_write(DDI_BUF_CTL_A, reg32);
 }
 
+/*
+ * Power the panel up, not its backlight, when the display is left to the OS
+ * at wake. An eDP panel raises HPD only once it has power (T3), and an OS can
+ * read the HPD state of the panel port before it powers the panel up itself:
+ * macOS does at wake, and keeps the display off when it finds it low. Force
+ * VDD on, as an OS driver does to reach the panel over AUX with the panel off,
+ * and wait for the power-up delay. The power sequence and the backlight stay
+ * off; Linux takes the forced VDD over ("VDD left on by BIOS").
+ */
+static void gma_panel_vdd_on(struct device *dev)
+{
+	const struct northbridge_intel_haswell_config *conf = config_of(dev);
+	const unsigned int up_delay_ms = conf->panel_cfg.up_delay_ms;
+	const u32 pp_control = gtt_read(PCH_PP_CONTROL);
+
+	/* No panel power sequence, or the panel has power already */
+	if (!up_delay_ms || (pp_control & (PANEL_POWER_ON | EDP_FORCE_VDD)))
+		return;
+
+	gtt_write(PCH_PP_CONTROL, pp_control | EDP_FORCE_VDD);
+	mdelay(up_delay_ms);
+}
+
 enum gpu_type {
 	GPU_TYPE_ULX,
 	GPU_TYPE_ULT,
@@ -692,7 +715,8 @@ static void gma_func0_init(struct device *dev)
 	/*
 	 * On S3 resume, unless asked to light the display up as at boot, leave
 	 * it to the graphics driver of the OS, as when a VBIOS is not run again
-	 * on resume: the panel setup above is all the firmware does.
+	 * on resume: the panel setup above is all the firmware does, with VDD
+	 * for the HPD of the panel.
 	 */
 	const bool display_to_os = acpi_is_wakeup_s3() &&
 				   !get_uint_option("gfx_resume_init", 1);
@@ -703,9 +727,11 @@ static void gma_func0_init(struct device *dev)
 			       "IGD is not decoding legacy VGA MEM and IO: skipping NATIVE graphic init\n");
 		} else if (display_to_os) {
 			printk(BIOS_INFO, "S3 resume: display left to the OS\n");
+			gma_panel_vdd_on(dev);
 			/* What the OS finds: the live HPD state, the panel power */
-			printk(BIOS_DEBUG, "GMA: SDEISR %08x, PP_STATUS %08x\n",
-			       gtt_read(SDEISR), gtt_read(PCH_PP_STATUS));
+			printk(BIOS_DEBUG, "GMA: SDEISR %08x PP_STATUS %08x PP_CONTROL %08x\n",
+			       gtt_read(SDEISR), gtt_read(PCH_PP_STATUS),
+			       gtt_read(PCH_PP_CONTROL));
 		} else {
 			printk(BIOS_SPEW, "NATIVE graphics, run native enable\n");
 			gma_gfxinit(&lightup_ok);
-- 
